. Oegema. <year>2004</year>. Centriole assembly requires both centriolar and pericentriolar material proteins. <source>Dev. Cell.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>815</fpage>&#x02013;829.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15572125</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Delattre, M., and P. Gonczy. <year>2004</year>. The arithmetic of centrosome biogenesis. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>1619</fpage>&#x02013;1629.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15075224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Dippell, R.V. <year>1968</year>. The development of basal bodies in paramecium. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>61</volume>:<fpage>461</fpage>&#x02013;468.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4176480</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Gaertig, J., M.A. Cruz, J. Bowen, L. Gu, D.G. Pennock, and M.A. Gorovsky. <year>1995</year>. Acetylation of lysine 40 in &#x003b1;-tubulin is not essential in <italic>Tetrahymena thermophila</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>129</volume>:<fpage>1301</fpage>&#x02013;1310.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7775576</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Hai, B., and M.A. Gorovsky. <year>1997</year>. Germ-line knockout heterokaryons of an essential &#x003b1;-tubulin gene enable high-frequency gene replacement and a test of gene transfer from somatic to germ-line in <italic>Tetrahymena thermophila</italic>. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>94</volume>:<fpage>1310</fpage>&#x02013;1315.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9037049</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Hendrickson, T.W., J. Yao, S. Bhadury, A.H. Corbett, and H.C. Joshi. <year>2001</year>. Conditional mutations in gamma-tubulin reveal its involvement in chromosome segregation and cytokinesis. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>2469</fpage>&#x02013;2481.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11514629</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Hinchcliffe, E.H., and G. Sluder. <year>2001</year>. Centrosome duplication: three kinases come up a winner. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>R698</fpage>&#x02013;R701.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11553343</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Incl&#x000e1;n, Y.F., and E. Nogales. <year>2001</year>. Structural models for the self-assembly and microtubule interactions of &#x003b3;-, &#x003b4;- and &#x0025b;-tubulin. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>413</fpage>&#x02013;422.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11148142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Jerka-Dziadosz, M., L.M. Jenkins, E.M. Nelsen, N.E. Williams, R. Jaeckel-Williams, and J. Frankel. <year>1995</year>. Cellular polarity in ciliates: persistence of global polarity in a disorganized mutant of <italic>Tetrahymena thermophila</italic> that disrupts cytoskeletal organization. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>169</volume>:<fpage>644</fpage>&#x02013;661.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7781905</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Jung, M.K., N. Prigozhina, C.E. Oakley, E. Nogales, and B.R. Oakley. <year>2001</year>. Alanine-scanning mutagenesis of <italic>Aspergillus</italic> gamma-tubulin yields diverse and novel phenotypes. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>2119</fpage>&#x02013;2136.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11452008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Kaczanowski, A. <year>1978</year>. Gradients of proliferation of ciliary basal bodies and the determination of the position of the oral primordium in <italic>Tetrahymena</italic>. <source>J. Exp. Zool.</source> <volume>204</volume>:<fpage>417</fpage>&#x02013;430.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">96207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Khodjakov, A., C.L. Rieder, G. Sluder, G. Cassels, O. Sibon, and C.L. Wang. <year>2002</year>. De novo formation of centrosomes in vertebrate cells arrested during S phase. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>158</volume>:<fpage>1171</fpage>&#x02013;1181.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12356862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">La Terra, S., C.N. English, P. Hergert, B.F. McEwen, G. Sluder, and A. Khodjakov. <year>2005</year>. The de novo centriole assembly pathway in HeLa cells: cell cycle progression and centriole assembly/maturation. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>168</volume>:<fpage>713</fpage>&#x02013;722.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15738265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Marshall, W.F., Y. Vucica, and J.L. Rosenbaum. <year>2001</year>. Kinetics and regulation of de novo centriole assembly. Implications for the mechanism of centriole duplication. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>308</fpage>&#x02013;317.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11267867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Matsumoto, Y., and J.L. Maller. <year>2002</year>. Calcium, calmodulin, and CaMKII requirement for initiation of centrosome duplication in <italic>Xenopus</italic> egg extracts. <source>Science.</source> <volume>295</volume>:<fpage>499</fpage>&#x02013;502.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11799245</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Nanney, D.L. <year>1975</year>. Patterns of basal body addition in ciliary rows in <italic>Tetrahymena</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>65</volume>:<fpage>503</fpage>&#x02013;512.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">805789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Nelsen, E.M., N.E. Williams, H. Yi, J. Knaak, and J. Frankel. <year>1994</year>. &#x0201c;Fenestrin&#x0201d; and conjugation in <italic>Tetrahymena thermophila</italic>. <source>J. Eukaryot. Microbiol.</source> <volume>41</volume>:<fpage>483</fpage>&#x02013;495.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7804251</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Nogales, E. <year>2001</year>. Structural insights into microtubule function. <source>Annu. Rev. Biophys. Biomol. Struct.</source> <volume>30</volume>:<fpage>397</fpage>&#x02013;420.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11441808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Nogales, E., S.G. Wolf, and K.H. Downing. <year>1998</year>. Structure of the &#x003b1;&#x003b2;tubulin dimer by electron crystallography. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>391</volume>:<fpage>199</fpage>&#x02013;203.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9428769</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Oakley, B.R. <year>2000</year>. &#x003b3;-Tubulin. <source>Curr. Top. Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>49</volume>:<fpage>27</fpage>&#x02013;54.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11005013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Oakley, C.E., and B.R. Oakley. <year>1989</year>. Identification of gamma-tubulin, a new member of the tubulin superfamily encoded by mipA gene of <italic>Aspergillus nidulans</italic>. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>338</volume>:<fpage>662</fpage>&#x02013;664.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2649796</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Orias, E., and L. Rasmussen. <year>1976</year>. Dual capacity for nutrient uptake in <italic>Tetrahymena</italic>. IV. Growth without food vacuoles and its implications. <source>Exp. Cell Res.</source> <volume>102</volume>:<fpage>127</fpage>&#x02013;137.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">824146</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Ruiz, F., J. Beisson, J. Rossier, and P. Dupuis-Williams. <year>1999</year>. Basal body duplication in <italic>Paramecium</italic> requires gamma-tubulin. <source>Cur